  "title": "6 · Storage, File Organisation & Indexing (Unit 4)",
  "learn": "<h3>Storage hierarchy</h3><p>Media differ in speed, cost and reliability. <b>Primary</b>: cache and main memory (fastest, most expensive, <b>volatile</b>). <b>Secondary</b>: flash and magnetic disk (non-volatile; flash reads fast but writes/erases slowly). <b>Tertiary</b>: optical disk and magnetic tape, used mainly for backups. Going down, cost falls and access time rises.</p>\n<h3>File organisation</h3><p>A database is a collection of <b>files</b>; a file is a sequence of <b>records</b>; a record is a sequence of <b>fields</b>. Data moves between disk and RAM in whole <b>blocks</b>. <b>Records per block = block size ÷ record size</b> (512 B ÷ 4 B = 128 records).</p>\n<p><b>Spanned</b>: a record may be split across blocks (no wasted space but reading one record may need two blocks). <b>Unspanned</b>: a record always sits in one block (block 10 B, record 3 B: 3 records fit and 1 B is wasted). Most databases use unspanned. Records can be <b>unordered</b> (fast insert, slow search) or <b>ordered</b> on an attribute.</p>\n<h3>Indexing</h3><p>An index reduces disk accesses. Each entry has a <b>search key</b> and a <b>data reference (pointer)</b> to a disk block. <b>Dense</b>: an entry for every search-key value. <b>Sparse</b>: entries for only some records. Example: SK 1→B1 (records 1-10), 11→B2, 21→B3, 31→B4; to find record 25, go straight to block 3.</p>\n<p><b>Single-level</b>: <b>primary</b> (ordered file, key), <b>clustering</b> (ordered file, non-key), <b>secondary</b> (unordered file). <b>Multilevel</b>: <b>B-tree</b> and <b>B+-tree</b>.</p><figure style=\"margin:14px 0\"><svg class=\"dg\" viewBox=\"0 0 580 262\"><defs><marker id=\"ar\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker><marker id=\"ar2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr2\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker></defs><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"0\" width=\"170\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"95.0\" y=\"22.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cache memory</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"192\" y=\"21\" text-anchor=\"start\">Primary: fastest, most expensive, volatile</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"170\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"95.0\" y=\"62.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Main memory (RAM)</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"192\" y=\"61\" text-anchor=\"start\">Primary: volatile</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"80\" width=\"170\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"95.0\" y=\"102.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Flash memory</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"192\" y=\"101\" text-anchor=\"start\">Secondary: non-volatile, fast read, slow write/erase</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"120\" width=\"170\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"95.0\" y=\"142.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Magnetic disk</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"192\" y=\"141\" text-anchor=\"start\">Secondary: large data, non-volatile</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"160\" width=\"170\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"95.0\" y=\"182.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Optical disk</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"192\" y=\"181\" text-anchor=\"start\">Tertiary</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"200\" width=\"170\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"95.0\" y=\"222.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Magnetic tape</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"192\" y=\"221\" text-anchor=\"start\">Tertiary: backups, huge volume</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"10\" y=\"258\" text-anchor=\"start\">going down: cost per byte falls, access time rises</text></svg><figcaption class=\"mu\" style=\"text-align:center\">Figure 16: storage hierarchy</figcaption></figure><figure style=\"margin:14px 0\"><svg class=\"dg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 150\"><defs><marker id=\"ar\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker><marker id=\"ar2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr2\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker></defs><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"10\" y=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\">Unspanned (block = 10 B, record = 3 B)</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"24\" width=\"30\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"25.0\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R1</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"40\" y=\"24\" width=\"30\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"55.0\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R2</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"70\" y=\"24\" width=\"30\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"85.0\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R3</text><rect class=\"dg-bad\" x=\"100\" y=\"24\" width=\"10\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"105.0\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"150\" y=\"24\" width=\"30\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"165.0\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R4</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"180\" y=\"24\" width=\"30\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"195.0\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R5</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"210\" y=\"24\" width=\"30\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"225.0\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R6</text><rect class=\"dg-bad\" x=\"240\" y=\"24\" width=\"10\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"245.0\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"10\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"start\">1 B wasted per block (red)</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"10\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"start\">Spanned (record may continue in the next block)</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"108\" width=\"30\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"25.0\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R1</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"40\" y=\"108\" width=\"30\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"55.0\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R2</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"70\" y=\"108\" width=\"30\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"85.0\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R3</text><rect class=\"dg-ok\" x=\"100\" y=\"108\" width=\"10\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"105.0\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R4</text><rect class=\"dg-ok\" x=\"150\" y=\"108\" width=\"20\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"160.0\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R4</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"170\" y=\"108\" width=\"30\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"185.0\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R5</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"200\" y=\"108\" width=\"30\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"215.0\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R6</text><rect class=\"dg-ok\" x=\"230\" y=\"108\" width=\"20\" height=\"26\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"240.0\" y=\"126\" text-anchor=\"middle\">R7</text><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"10\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"start\">no waste, but reading R4 needs two blocks</text></svg><figcaption class=\"mu\" style=\"text-align:center\">Figure 17: unspanned vs spanned records</figcaption></figure><figure style=\"margin:14px 0\"><svg class=\"dg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 170\"><defs><marker id=\"ar\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker><marker id=\"ar2\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path class=\"dg-arr2\" d=\"M0,0L9,4.5L0,9z\"/></marker></defs><rect class=\"dg-hd\" x=\"10\" y=\"0\" width=\"70\" height=\"28\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"45.0\" y=\"19.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Key</text><rect class=\"dg-hd\" x=\"80\" y=\"0\" width=\"70\" height=\"28\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"115.0\" y=\"19.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Block</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"28\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"45.0\" y=\"48.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"80\" y=\"28\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"115.0\" y=\"48.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B1</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"260\" y=\"28\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"325.0\" y=\"48.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B1: records 1-10</text><line class=\"dg-ln\" x1=\"152\" y1=\"43\" x2=\"258\" y2=\"43\" marker-end=\"url(#ar)\"/><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"62\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"45.0\" y=\"82.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">11</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"80\" y=\"62\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"115.0\" y=\"82.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B2</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"260\" y=\"62\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"325.0\" y=\"82.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B2: records 11-20</text><line class=\"dg-ln\" x1=\"152\" y1=\"77\" x2=\"258\" y2=\"77\" marker-end=\"url(#ar)\"/><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"96\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"45.0\" y=\"116.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">21</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"80\" y=\"96\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"115.0\" y=\"116.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B3</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"260\" y=\"96\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"325.0\" y=\"116.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B3: records 21-30</text><line class=\"dg-r\" x1=\"152\" y1=\"111\" x2=\"258\" y2=\"111\" marker-end=\"url(#ar2)\"/><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"10\" y=\"130\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"45.0\" y=\"150.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">31</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"80\" y=\"130\" width=\"70\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"115.0\" y=\"150.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B4</text><rect class=\"dg-box\" x=\"260\" y=\"130\" width=\"130\" height=\"30\" rx=\"8\"/><text class=\"dg-t\" x=\"325.0\" y=\"150.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B4: records 31-40</text><line class=\"dg-ln\" x1=\"152\" y1=\"145\" x2=\"258\" y2=\"145\" marker-end=\"url(#ar)\"/><text class=\"dg-m\" x=\"10\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"start\">find record 25: key 21 → block B3 (red arrow)</text></svg><figcaption class=\"mu\" style=\"text-align:center\">Figure 18: a sparse single-level index (one entry per block)</figcaption></figure><h3>How files sit on disk</h3><p>Files can be stored in <b>contiguous</b> (sequential) allocation, <b>non-contiguous</b> allocation or <b>index allocation</b>. The CPU asks main memory (RAM); if the data is not there, a <b>whole block</b> is read from the hard disk into RAM, never a single bit or record. Unsorted files make insert and delete easy but search slow; sorted files make search fast.</p>",
